===Etymology===
{{etymon|fr|id=noun|inh|fro>compaing>noun|tree=1}}
# {{inh+|fr|fro|compaing}}, {{m|fro|compain|g=m}}, from {{inh|fr|LL.|compāniō|g=m}} (nominative form) (compare also {{cog|it|compagno|g=m}}), from {{af|la|com-|pānis|nocat=1|lit=with-bread|g2=m}}, a word first attested in the {{der|fr|frk|-}} ''Lex Salica'' as a translation of a {{der|fr|gem|-}} word, probably {{der|fr|frk|*galaibo}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*gahlaibō||messmate|lit=with-bread}}, from {{m|gmw-pro|*hlaib|g=m||loaf, bread}}. See also {{m|fr|compagnon|g=m}}, from the accusative form of the same Late Latin term {{m|la|compāniōnem}}, whence English {{m|en|companion}}.
# The sense of 'boyfriend' is by ellipsis of {{m|fr|petit copain}}.

